#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:93
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:95
msgid ""
"This driver supports hardware monitoring for various PMBus compliant "
"devices. It supports voltage, current, power, and temperature sensors as "
"supported by the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:99
msgid ""
"Each monitored channel has its own high and low limits, plus a critical "
"limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:102
msgid "Fan support will be added in a later version of this driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:106
msgid "Usage Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:108
msgid ""
"This driver does not probe for PMBus devices, since there is no register "
"which can be safely used to identify the chip (The MFG_ID register is not "
"supported by all chips), and since there is no well defined address range "
"for PMBus devices. You will have to instantiate the devices explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:113
msgid ""
"Example: the following will load the driver for an LTC2978 at address 0x60 "
"on I2C bus #1::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:121
msgid "Platform data support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:123
msgid ""
"Support for additional PMBus chips can be added by defining chip parameters "
"in a new chip specific driver file. For example, (untested) code to add "
"support for Emerson DS1200 power modules might look as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:183
msgid "Sysfs entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/pmbus.rst:185
msgid ""
"When probing the chip, the driver identifies which PMBus registers are "
"supported, and determines available sensors from this information. Attribute "
"files only exist if respective sensors are supported by the chip. Labels are "
"provided to inform the user about the sensor associated with a given sysfs "
"entry."
msgstr ""

